    <td>PINNACLE</td>\n                <td>₦1,650.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>DANGOTE</td>\n                <td>₦1,651.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>ZAMSON</td>\n                <td>₦1,670.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>RAINOIL DELTA</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>SIGMUND</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MATRIX WARRI</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>MATRIX PH</td>\n                <td>₦1,680.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n            <tr>\n                <td>IBETO</td>\n                <td>₦1,630.00</td>\n            </tr>\n            \n\n        </table>\n\n        <br>\n        \n\n            \n        <h2 style=\"color:#d42e12;\">\n            Market News\n        </h2>\n        \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Nigeria's Refining Capacity Could Hit 2.6m bpd by 2030\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigeria's domestic refining capacity could rise to 2.64 million barrels per day by the end of 2030. 24 new refinery projects progress through various stages of development. $10.74 billion worth of investments in modular refinery projects are expected to be completed between 2026 and 2030.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/nigerias-refining-capacity-could-hit-26m-bpd-by-2030\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Oil Prices Slip Below $88 as Hormuz Traffic Eases, But Monthly Rally Nears 20%\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Brent crude traded at $87.33 per barrel, down 1.91 per cent, while the US West Texas Intermediate (WTI) benchmark fell 2.19 per cent to $81.76 per barrel. Oil prices have softened over the past two trading sessions as more tankers resumed transiting the Strait of Hormuz.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/oil-prices-slip-below-88-as-hormuz-traffic-eases-but-monthly-rally-nears-20\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    FG to Reveal Fuel Subsidy Savings After Months of Public Pressure\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    The Federal Government has announced plans to publish a detailed report outlining savings realised from the removal of petrol and foreign exchange subsidies. The Minister of Finance and Coordinating Minister of the Economy, Taiwo Oyedele, disclosed this on Thursday at the 7th Africa Emerging Markets Forum in Abuja. He said the report would provide Nigerians with a comprehensive breakdown of the savings and how the resources have been deployed.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/fg-to-reveal-fuel-subsidy-savings-after-months-of-public-pressure\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    Diesel Supply Emerges as Biggest Risk to Global Oil Market — Goldman Sachs\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Goldman Sachs said diesel is now at the centre of the current fuel supply tightness. The investment bank said refinery outages and reduced operating rates weighing more heavily on refined product markets than on crude oil supplies.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/diesel-supply-emerges-as-biggest-risk-to-global-oil-market-goldman-sachs\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n            <div\n                style=\"\n                    border:1px solid #fad5a1;\n                    padding:15px;\n                    margin-bottom:15px;\n                    border-radius:8px;\n                    \n                \"\n            >\n\n                <h3>\n                    NMDPRA Seeks African Fuel Price Benchmark to Reduce Dependence on Foreign Indices\n                </h3>\n\n                <p>\n                    Nigerian Midstream and Downstream Petroleum Regulatory Authority has called for the development of an African fuel pricing benchmark. The Authority's Chief Executive, Rabiu Umar, said Africa remains one of the few major energy-producing regions without a recognised regional pricing benchmark, despite growing investments in refining and downstream infrastructure.\n                </p>\n\n                <a\n                    href=\"https://petroleumprice.ng/news/articles/nmdpra-seeks-african-fuel-price-benchmark-to-reduce-dependence-on-foreign-indices\"\n                    target=\"_blank\"\n                    style=\"\n                        color:#d42e12;\n                        font-weight:bold;\n                        text-decoration:none;\n                    \"\n                >\n                    Full Article →\n                </a>\n\n            </div>\n            \n\n        </body>\n\n        </html>\n        "
